{"declarations":[{"axioms":["propext","Classical.choice","Quot.sound"],"dependency_source":"lean_report","doc":"The property list of **Lemma 3.1** (`cc:uf:exact:lem:profile`,\nsections/04_localized_wave.tex:152) for a family `F h` of profiles and a family\n`P h` of primitives, `0 < h ≤ 1`: `F h` is odd, smooth and `1`-periodic, `P h`\nis a smooth `1`-periodic primitive of `F h` with zero mean over a period,\n`F_h'(0) = 1`, `-C h ≤ F_h' ≤ 1`, `‖F_h‖_∞ ≤ C h`, and\n`‖∂_s^j F_h‖_∞ ≤ C_j h^{1-j}` for `j ≥ 2`, with `C` and `C_j` independent of\n`h`.\n\nRepresentation: the supremum bounds are stated pointwise in the phase `s`;\n`phaseMean` is the integral over `[0,1]`.","end_line":52,"kind":"def","line":44,"module":"TorusEuler.Paper.S34A.Vocabulary","name":"TorusEuler.Paper.ProfileFamily","namespace":"TorusEuler.Paper","noncomputable":false,"noncomputable_section":true,"private":false,"proof_used_by":[],"proof_uses":[],"protected":false,"short":"ProfileFamily","signature_end_line":44,"sorry":false,"statement_used_by":["TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_3_1"],"statement_uses":["TorusEuler.phaseMean"],"used_by":["TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_3_1"],"uses":["TorusEuler.phaseMean"],"written":"ProfileFamily"},{"axioms":["propext","Classical.choice","Quot.sound"],"dependency_source":"lean_report","doc":"The standing setting of Section 4 (sections/06b_mean_inverse.tex:8–10):\n`0 < T ≤ 1`, the parent `U` is a smooth divergence-free field on\n`[0,T] × 𝕋³` (not assumed to solve any equation), and `X` is its flow.\n\nRepresentation: `U` is `ℤ³`-periodic on `ℝ³` and smooth on the closed slab\n`[0,T] × ℝ³`; the flow is the two-time label flow `IsLabelFlowOn U X [0,T]`,\nwhich contains the flow `X(t,a) = X 0 t a` and its inverse `X t 0`. The flow is\nvolume preserving because `U` is divergence free.","end_line":70,"kind":"structure","line":64,"module":"TorusEuler.Paper.S34A.Vocabulary","name":"TorusEuler.Paper.MeanParentFlow","namespace":"TorusEuler.Paper","noncomputable":false,"nonc