.tex:30–33):\n`K z_t - ∫_0^t Ω z_t + L = c + ∇φ`, `div z = 0`, `z(0) = z(T) = 0`, with\n`z ∈ C¹(I; C^{0,1/2})`, `c ∈ C^{0,1/2}` divergence free and\n`∇φ ∈ C(I; C^{0,1/2})`.\n\nRepresentation: `C^{0,1/2}` is the space `HalfHolder (UnitAddTorus (Fin 3)) Vec3`\n(maximum of the supremum and the `1/2`-seminorm). The displacement `z` and its\nvelocity `v = z_t` take values in the closed subspace\n`endpointHalfHolderSolenoidal` of weakly divergence-free fields, which encodes\n`div z = 0` and `div c = 0`; `z ∈ C¹` is the derivative `v` of `z` within `I`\ntogether with continuity of `v`. The pressure gradient is a continuous curve\n`G` in `C^{0,1/2}` whose lift is the gradient of the periodic potential `φ t`.\nThe left side of the equation is `paperMeanIntegratedMomentum K Ω L v t`\n`= K(t)v(t) - ∫_0^t Ω(s)v(s) ds + L(t)`, with pointwise coefficient\nmultiplication.","end_line":134,"kind":"structure","line":125,"module":"TorusEuler.Paper.S34A.Vocabulary","name":"TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution","namespace":"TorusEuler.Paper","noncomputable":false,"noncomputable_section":true,"private":false,"proof_used_by":["TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S5a.meanUnique_of_theorem42"],"proof_uses":[],"protected":false,"short":"EndpointSystemSolution","signature_end_line":126,"sorry":false,"statement_used_by":["TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.displacement_deriv","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.equation","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.gradient_continuous","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.initial","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.potential","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.terminal","TorusEuler.Paper.EndpointSystemSolution.velocity_continuous","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S34A.A1Body","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S34A.EndpointSystemSolution.congr","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S34A.endpointSystemSolution_scale","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S34A.smooth42","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S34A.solve42","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S5a.Tower.main_tower_bound","TorusEuler.Paper.Lib.S5a.Tower.zero